<h1>Lua API reference</h1>
<p>Import every engine service with <code>require("demi.…")</code>. Each call is a plain Lua function on the imported table — store the module in a local and call through it.</p>
<pre><code>local Transform3D = require("demi.transform3d")
local x, y, z = Transform3D.get_position("player")</code></pre>

<h2>How values come back</h2>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Shape</th><th>Used by</th><th>How to read it</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><code>local x, y, z = …</code></td>
      <td>Transform positions, rotations, scales, velocities</td>
      <td>Multiple scalar returns. Assign exactly as many names as the function reports, or the extras are <code>nil</code>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>{x, y}</code> / <code>{x, y, z}</code></td>
      <td>Embedded vectors in tables (hits, specs, spawn options) and <code>demi.math.vector2</code>/<code>vector3</code> results</td>
      <td>Fixed-length numeric arrays. Index with <code>v[1]</code>, <code>v[2]</code>, <code>v[3]</code> (Lua arrays start at 1).</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>value, nil</code> / <code>nil, err</code></td>
      <td><code>Data.load</code>, <code>Http.request</code>, path queries</td>
      <td>Check the first result. On failure the second result is a table describing the problem.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>nil</code></td>
      <td>Missed raycasts, missing entities, unknown nodes</td>
      <td>Guard with <code>if hit then … end</code> before reading fields.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>{}</code></td>
      <td>Overlap queries, event batches, children lists</td>
      <td>An empty array means “nothing found”, not an error. Use <code>ipairs</code>.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Units</h2>
<ul>
  <li><code>Transform2D</code> rotation and <code>Transform3D</code> Euler rotation: <strong>radians</strong>.</li>
  <li>Rigidbody angular velocity: <strong>radians per second</strong>.</li>
  <li>Camera FOV: <strong>degrees</strong>.</li>
  <li><code>Time.delta_time</code>, <code>Time.fixed_time</code>: <strong>seconds</strong>.</li>
  <li>HUD positions and sizes: <strong>canvas units</strong> from the HUD document <code>canvas_size</code>.</li>
</ul>

